MID_SE_Lil_Moo_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Lil_Moo_C_001: Mmghhh.
MID_SE_Lil_Moo_C_002: What's wrong, Lilian? You not feeling good?
MID_SE_Lil_Moo_C_003: It's my head. I didn't catch anything when I was out\nhunting, so I went without dinner.
MID_SE_Lil_Moo_C_004: You shouldn't overdo it when you feel sick. Maybe\nyou can go to an inn and get some rest.
MID_SE_Lil_Moo_C_005: Pass. I'm trying to save money.
MID_SE_Lil_Moo_C_006: But if you don't start feeling better, you'll have\nanother bad hunt, right?
MID_SE_Lil_Moo_C_007: Ouch. Way to kick me when I'm down. Look, it'll\npass if I can just get some sleep.
MID_SE_Lil_Moo_C_008: Augh... That— Hey, sorry to ask, but could you get\nme some water?
MID_SE_Lil_Moo_C_009: Sure. I'll be right back.
MID_SE_Lil_Moo_C_010: She's taking her sweet time with that water.
MID_SE_Lil_Moo_C_011: Sorry it took me so long! I made you some food, but\nit's nothing fancy.
MID_SE_Lil_Moo_C_012: You cooked? But all I wanted was water.
MID_SE_Lil_Moo_C_013: You haven't eaten, right? Come on, you have to\nput something in your stomach.
MID_SE_Lil_Moo_C_014: Damn, you went all out with this. How much do I\nowe you?
MID_SE_Lil_Moo_C_015: I don't want your money—I just wanna know how it\ntastes. It's a new version of a dish I'm working on.
MID_SE_Lil_Moo_C_016: I've tried it myself, but I really need someone\nelse to test it on.
MID_SE_Lil_Moo_C_017: Mmm! If you say so. Thanks. Now excuse me while\nI chow...down?
MID_SE_Lil_Moo_C_018: You're sure this is food for people, right?
MID_SE_Lil_Moo_C_019: Of course. I mean, of all the dishes I make, this one\nprobably tastes the best.
MID_SE_Lil_Moo_C_020: Though, it sounds like you don't really like it.\nI'll just take it away.
MID_SE_Lil_Moo_C_021: No, no! Wouldn't wanna waste food. Especially when\nit's free.
MID_SE_Lil_Moo_C_022: You don't have to eat it. Really. Your head hurts—\nplus I'm used to eating it, so I'll just have it later.
MID_SE_Lil_Moo_C_023: I'm telling you it's fine. I'm gonna clean this plate.\nUh... Once I get feeling back in my tongue.
MID_SE_Lil_Moo_C_024: Are you OK, Lilian? You really don't have to\nforce yourself. It's an...acquired taste.
MID_SE_Lil_Moo_C_025: But you made it just for me. I'd feel bad for the food\nif I tossed it. Ow...
MID_SE_Lil_Moo_C_026: Y'know, maybe I can't do this. Sorry. Let's say you've\ndone enough for me, alright?
MID_SE_Lil_Moo_C_027: I think my dish just made things worse.
MID_SE_Lil_Moo_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Lil_Moo_B_001: Hey there. I was looking for you so I could thank you\nfor the free meal.
MID_SE_Lil_Moo_B_002: What? Why? Eating my food made you sick.
MID_SE_Lil_Moo_B_003: Yeah, but my head felt fine right afterward. Better\nthan fine, actually.
MID_SE_Lil_Moo_B_004: Which seemed strange, so I figured your food had\nsomething to do with it.
MID_SE_Lil_Moo_B_005: Yes! Great! I'm so glad it worked on you too, Lilian.
MID_SE_Lil_Moo_B_006: The dish fixes headaches. I created it by accident.\nI just threw some stuff together, and...it worked!
MID_SE_Lil_Moo_B_007: At first it tasted awful, but I did some experimenting\nwith the recipe and eventually made it more edible.
MID_SE_Lil_Moo_B_008: Hold up. It used to taste worse?
MID_SE_Lil_Moo_B_009: Yeah, it tasted like soap. Or maybe copper? It was so\nbitter, and I couldn't taste anything else for a while.
MID_SE_Lil_Moo_B_010: How often do you do this to yourself?
MID_SE_Lil_Moo_B_011: Well, I guess I do it when I think I can help people.\nThat's how I fixed your headache, isn't it?
MID_SE_Lil_Moo_B_012: I should probably try to stop you, but I doubt\nit'd do any good.
MID_SE_Lil_Moo_B_013: So instead, I'll join you. If I'm around, I can at least\nsee what you're putting in this stuff.
MID_SE_Lil_Moo_B_014: And if we take turns testing it, then when one of us\npasses out, the other can go get help.
MID_SE_Lil_Moo_B_015: What, you mean it?! You'd do that for me?!
MID_SE_Lil_Moo_B_016: Sure. It'll cut back on my food budget and keep me\nin good enough shape to work more.
MID_SE_Lil_Moo_B_017: Haha! It always comes down to money for you.\nYou sure are practical.
MID_SE_Lil_Moo_B_018: Still, I'm happy to have a new cooking buddy! Would\nyou mind helping me out, say...right now?
MID_SE_Lil_Moo_B_019: I didn't have any other plans, so sure. What are we\ntrying to make today?
MID_SE_Lil_Moo_B_020: A traditional dish with mashed potatoes and spices.\nBut I want to experiment with some new flavors!
MID_SE_Lil_Moo_B_021: There are these pyrethrums that grow near here,\nso I thought we could try adding some.
MID_SE_Lil_Moo_B_022: What, those nasty flowers? People grind them up to\nmake insect repellent.
MID_SE_Lil_Moo_B_023: I accidentally got one in my mouth once. It numbed\nmy tongue, but not before tasting awful.
MID_SE_Lil_Moo_B_024: Ah, don't worry. I bet if we mix those flowers with\nother spices, the taste will be super unique.
MID_SE_Lil_Moo_B_025: Says who? Ughhh. I'm getting a headache all\nover again.
MID_SE_Lil_Moo_B_026: Oooh, perfect! I'll start making my special headache-\nhealing dish. I've improved on it since last time!
MID_SE_Lil_Moo_B_027: Wait, Mu! I was kidding! All better now!